content.text:
The Home and first-chat subagent stopped partway because the ChatGPT plan's usage limit ran out (it resets at 2:01 PM). I restarted the work on Opus 5.5 as [Finish Home and first chat speed](t3-thread://v2/88042f69-c439-49f6-a4b9-1fb5180f2502/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A69847fef-da96-4810-b2ac-2bb541d41be3%3Adelegate-task%3A882d4d48-d227-4fb9-9167-73ff726d939c). It continues from the previous agent's three commits and its unfinished chat-route edits, which I saved as a patch.

The previous agent had already changed Home to show the heading first and the dashboard grid once the net-worth figure is ready, so the mobile layout doesn't jump. The new agent's job is to confirm that against the base build:
- page timings in the browser and on the server;
- no new layout shift on mobile;
- net worth and balances exactly the same as before;
- time to the first chat reply, with the AI mocked so nothing costs money.

Then it opens a PR into `t3/speed-build-and-startup`.

The desktop cold-start subagent is still working too. The next tasks stay on Claude models until the ChatGPT limit resets.

